    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23-a1">

                <pb facs="0135" n="108" xml:id="pg108"/>


                <head>Talking Points Prepared in the National Security Council<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d23-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian">undated</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">POINTS TO BE MADE FOR MEETING WITH
                        THE NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>—</label>
                    <item>Your people have done an excellent job in focusing a very broad and
                        difficult review of the arms control implications of our defense strategy
                        into the questions we are to address today. I’ve said it before, but need to
                        say it again: Please convey to your staffs my thanks for the long hours and
                        enormous effort they have put into this study.</item>
                    <label>—</label>
                    <item>Today will be our first of many opportunities to discuss arms control. The
                        issues are tough, but we need to face up to them at the outset.</item>
                    <label>—</label>
                    <item>I want to use today to have a frank and candid discussion about the
                        premises and policies that underpin our positions in the START and Defense
                        and Space Talks. I want to ensure we are clear about where we are headed and
                        that we have chosen the best road to get there.</item>
                    <label>—</label>
                    <item>That is the only way we can develop sound negotiating positions, achieve
                        arms control agreements that are in our interest, and sustain the support we
                        will need to ratify them.</item>
                    <label>—</label>
                    <item>Brent, let me ask you to introduce each of the issues in turn.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
